      "type": "text",
      "text": "I can't submit this order. I don't have an order entry system connected in this session, so nothing has been entered, and I don't want you to assume it has been. You'll need to place it in your EHR's CPOE yourself.\n\nSince you're ordering above the labeled maximum, I'd suggest these steps:\n\n1. **Document the indication and rationale.** You haven't told me why 400 mg is intended, and the order should carry that reasoning.\n2. **Get attending sign-off,** ideally before release, and expect a pharmacy dose-range alert. Pharmacy may call to verify, which is appropriate.\n3. **Reconcile interacting drugs** (serotonergic agents, QT-prolonging drugs) and consider a baseline ECG and sodium level.\n4. **Set monitoring** for serotonin toxicity signs (agitation, tremor, clonus, hyperthermia, diarrhea), QTc, and sodium.\n\nHere is the order text you can paste or adapt:\n\n> **Sertraline 400 mg PO once daily.** Dose exceeds labeled max (200 mg/day). Indication: [___]. Rationale for supratherapeutic dose: [___]. Reviewed with attending [name]. Baseline ECG/Na: [___]. Monitor for serotonin toxicity, QTc prolongation, hyponatremia.\n\nIf the dose was meant to be a titration target, an alternative is ordering the current step (e.g., 100-200 mg daily) with a documented titration plan. I can help draft that if useful."
     }
