   "result": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the maximum. Sertraline's labeled maximum for adults is **200 mg/day**, and 400 mg once daily is double that. Higher doses carry a greater risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and hyponatremia, and they haven't shown added benefit. Normal renal and hepatic function and no allergies don't change that ceiling.\n\nCould you clarify which of these you intended?\n\n- **A typo or unit slip:** for example, 40 mg or 100 mg daily. Typical dosing is 25-50 mg daily to start for depression or anxiety, titrated by 25-50 mg weekly or less often, up to 200 mg.\n- **A deliberate dose above the labeled max:** if so, I'd want the indication and rationale documented, and the order would probably need attending or pharmacy review before it's released.\n- **A different drug or formulation:** for example, if you meant a different medication.\n\nAlso check the patient's other medications for serotonergic agents (linezolid, tramadol, triptans, other SSRIs/SNRIs, MAOIs) and QT-prolonging drugs, since those interactions matter even at standard doses.\n\nTell me the corrected dose, or confirm that 400 mg is intentional along with the indication, and I'll proceed. I'll also need frequency, start time, and any hold parameters if you want them included.",
